Third-party media tools (not distributed in the UTD installer)
---------------------------------------------------------------
UTD uses a yt-dlp or ffmpeg that is already installed on the computer
(UTD's own tools folder, PATH, WinGet, Scoop or Chocolatey). Only when the
user clicks "Tải yt-dlp", "Tải ffmpeg" or "Cập nhật" in Settings does UTD
download the tool from its upstream GitHub release over HTTPS, check its
SHA-256 against the checksum file published in the same release, and place
it in %LOCALAPPDATA%\UTD-Data\bin. Nothing is downloaded otherwise.

- yt-dlp (https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp): released under the Unlicense.
  The Windows yt-dlp.exe build bundles third-party components, some under
  GPLv3+; see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt in the yt-dlp repository.
- FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), Windows "win64-gpl" builds from
  https://github.com/yt-dlp/FFmpeg-Builds: licensed under the GNU GPL
  version 3. The build's LICENSE.txt is copied next to the binaries as
  ffmpeg-LICENSE.txt. Source code is available from FFmpeg and from the
  FFmpeg-Builds repository.

UTD runs these tools as separate processes and does not link to them.
